    "videoId": "r3UXC_U6iCQ",
    "title": "Are Older G's Still Worthwhile?",
    "lengthSeconds": "709",
    "channelId": "UCv6W0sNee2SpYlqUXb0GOiw",
    "isOwnerViewing": false,
    "shortDescription": "The early 2000s G Wagons don’t always get the attention they deserve, but they can still represent one of the best ways to get into a proper G—if you know what you’re looking at.\n\nIn this video, we break down what makes these G’s worth considering and some of the things you should inspect before buying one. We’ll cover everything from the condition of the leather and interior to common places to look for rust, along with the engines, performance, and what these trucks are actually like to own and drive more than two decades later.\n\nAge alone doesn’t make a G Wagon a bad buy. In a lot of cases, these trucks have plenty of life left in them, and there are some very good reasons to shop this era instead of immediately jumping to something newer.\n\nIf you’re considering an early-2000s G and have questions, give Nothing But G’s a call. And if you’d rather have someone who knows these trucks help you find the right one, we can do that too.\n\n[email redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n@nothingbutgs on Instagram\n\n827 S. Lincoln Ave., Loveland, CO 80537",
